check the mic and make sure it sound  right boy  it's been 20 long years since claude a  mute criminal was double-crossed by his  girlfriend and sent to prison in the  original gta 3. that game changed how  open world video games were made and the  subsequent games in the series vice city  and san andreas became two of the most  loved games in history and now all three  games are back for some well-needed  nostalgia and for a whole new generation  of gamers to understand what all the  fuss was about back then i'm gonna break  this video into two sections first all  the updates that have come to the games  after all these years then we'll break  down what each game does differently and  hopefully you can do me a favor and let  me know which game you'd like videos  based around first i'm adam and this is  20 things you need to know about the gta  trilogy definitive edition  let's start with a quick note the  definitive edition of gta has two  release dates for everyone who likes  digital games november the 11th is the  day we can start playing but if you  prefer physical games ones you can touch  maybe for our christmas present be aware  that these don't release until december  the 7th on subscription services ps now  subs can play the original gta 3 from  december the 7th and those on game pass  have a way better deal you can play san  andreas on release day this thursday the  grand theft auto trilogy is a remaster  and not a remake and by looking at the  early footage it's very easy to see why  all three games keep their og look but  they have been forced into modern times  with a few little tricks the character  models have been updated to look  acceptable but what the real advancement  here is the lighting headlights on  vehicles pop neons glow on the side of  buildings and explosions rip through the  air under the hood the updates are far  more important and impressive back in  2004 can you guess which button on a  controller we use to fire a weapon  circle that's right on a ps2 controller  we used circle and it was b on xbox  which is why we all played claw back  then and messed up our hands together of  course the modern way is to use the  shoulder triggers and the bumpers and  thankfully this has been rectified in  the trilogy as all games use the control  scheme perfected in gta 5. this includes  the revolutionary weapon wheel so if  you're playing gta online you can still  play vice city without needing to switch  button layouts  there's a few smaller updates too which  include the ability to place waypoints  on the map wow the early 2000s were  tough on us gamers we had to learn the  streets and navigate without gps  probably the greatest update to the  entire trilogy is that of immediately  restarting a mission if and when you  fail this may seem a simple update but  back then if we failed we had to get our  sorry butts all the way back across the  map to activate the mission again sit  through the cutscene again and then go  all the way back to where we just failed  the mission again it was hell but at  least it spawned a meme all we had to do  was follow the damn train cj we had to  do was follow the damn train cj all we  had to do was follow the damn train cj  follow the damn train cj another  important update is to draw distance gta  3 vice city and especially san andreas  had issues loading in scenery fast  enough at times it was like silent hill  waiting for buildings to load in 30 feet  away from us the definitive edition has  solved this issue and the draw distances  have been modernized and now should  operate much more like gta online with  low res textures seamlessly  transitioning to upscale resolution  textures as we get closer and if you're  on ps5 or xbox series x you can have all  this at 4k 60 frames a second  so now the real question which are you  going to play first here's a bunch of  things i found out about gta 3 vice city  and san andreas if you're a fan of  setting and story here's a super quick  breakdown of each game gta 3 is set in a  fictional new york city named liberty  city we play as claude a mute  protagonist who is arrested after being  set up by his girlfriend claude breaks  out of the prison transport with other  cons and eventually becomes a mafia  enforcer and wheel man in the seedy  underworld of liberty city always hoping  that he will once again see the woman  who tricked him gta vice city takes us  back in time to the mid-1980s the  liberty city mafia families are  expanding tommy vercetti is freshly  released from prison and sent to miami  aka vice city to establish a drug  operation there things go as wrong as  they can and tommy is left for dead it's  our job to build him back up to become  the scarface of vice city the undisputed  kingpin  vice city was actually the first gta  game with a fully voiced main character  and it was played by ray liotta  channeling his character from the  goodfellas movie gta san andreas takes  place in the 1990s in california los  santos is los angeles san fierro is san  francisco and les venturas is las vegas  in nevada we play as cj who returns home  after his mother is killed in a drive-by  shooting in the ganglands cj barely gets  time to grieve before he's immediately  forced to do the bidding of the local  police department he is framed for a  recent murder and should he not do what  they say they will send him to prison  and by the way the dirty cop is played  by samuel l jackson circle while doing  the bidding for officer 10 penny cj also  helps his childhood friends grow their  territory and commit quite a lot of  crimes out of the three games gta 3 is  the shortest taking about 15 hours to  complete the story missions there are 51  in total but for a completionist run  you'll need about 40 hours to finish the  full 77 missions and side missions next  is vice city which will take the average  gamer 20 hours to finish the 38 story  missions the thing is there is another  49 missible missions for the  completionist in you which will take  about 40 hours for a full playthrough of  all content and now the big boy san  andreas has 101 story missions to finish  the game making the average play through  about 30 hours the thing is san andreas  has countless side missions which are  replayable making the estimate to do  everything in san andreas a whopping 80  hours of your time grand theft auto san  andreas was so revolutionary at the time  we could become a firefighter and go on  calls to extinguish fires we could  become a courier and deliver parcels all  day there is even the ability to take a  crew on a burglary mission at night to  rob the rich folk san andreas included a  gang war mechanic which let the grove  street families take over areas of the  map using brute force they could also  lose that territory if they weren't  protecting it well enough i'll warn you  now watching the map turn green is  addictive but without a doubt the  greatest ever update to a gta game comes  in san andreas and it's all about food  cj puts in his body it's possible to  make carl obese i mean wow really a  beast it actually stunts his performance  he's he can run far less he can barely  leap fences and worst of all some  characters will flat out refuse to work  with him until he loses weight cj can  put this right by eating correctly and  visiting the gym  thick cj could become hench cj which  also feeds into a sex appeal mechanic in  the game cj can  caught ladies shall we say and each of  them likes a certain physique most of  them like thin or muscles but some of  the dirty gals like a big fat cj more  cushion for the pushing  i should stop talking now the fat thin  mechanic and the sex appeal and  mechanics weren't implemented in gta 4  and 5 making san andreas one of the most  unique gta games in history and to end  all this here are the maps for each of  the games and let's compare them to  other gta games the land mass in gta 3  is 4.38 kilometers squared which  compared to gta 5 is tiny gta 5 has a  massive land mass of 48 squared  kilometers vice city is 5.62 kilometers  squared and then take a look at san  andreas a massive 31.5 squared  kilometers of landmass this is so huge  it's actually bigger than gta 4 by a  long way so now i leave it to you which  game are you playing first with over 160  hours of gameplay across the three games  it doesn't matter that gta 6 probably  won't be here for another five years we  have lots to do in the meantime  i'm adam thank you for sticking around  till the end much appreciated which game  are you playing first i'm thinking vice  city what about you it's been a pleasure  i'll see you next time  [Music]  [Applause]

